module v2.std.compilers.lowered_shape

// WHICH PRODUCER LOWERED A NODE IS A FACT OF ITS CONSTRUCTION, NOT A READING OF ITS SHAPE (MQ-5,
// neat-boar-16 ruling 2026-09-30, option A; realized as the operator-approved interim B, msg_63aee66e).
// Body lowering is a bottom-up fold over a tree that holds raw parse and lowered output at once, and
// nothing on a Node says which is which, so every reader used to ask a hand-kept shape allowlist
// (body_lower_is_core_substrate) and re-read anything it missed as raw parse. Each producer now
// declares what it built: its result leaves the producer inside the stage's Lowered wrapper, carrying
// one of these arms as a constant the producer writes, and a reader matches the term
// (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_term_of) instead of classifying the node. The arms name the
// producer family that built the value.
// WHO READS THE ARM, STATED AS IT IS (review 76884; DESIGN section 3c). In this change the SEAL is
// consumed -- body_term_of keys Lowered versus RawParse/RawLeaf on its presence -- and the arm it
// carries is not: every reader takes a Lowered term whole (shape: _). That is a declared frontier,
// not a consumer. Its named consumer is the stage ceiling body_lowering_fold states beside the seal:
// a sealed BodyTerm term tree that normalize consumes by dispatching on the producer arm instead of
// re-reading node shapes (MQ-6). TRIGGER: that change lands its first normalize match over
// LoweredShape. If it does not, this arm collapses to a unit seal -- the discriminator alone is what
// this change needs -- rather than staying as data nothing reads.
// It sits in its own module, below v2.std.node, because the seal on the Lowered wrapper's edge
// carries it (v2.std.node BodyTermLoweredSeal): the seal holds the closed shape itself, so no
// symbol round-trip, roster list or unknown-shape arm exists to drift from this declaration.
type LoweredShape
  = LoweredOperatorExpression
  | LoweredFunctionValue
  | LoweredFoldEncoding
  | LoweredMatch
  | LoweredBranch
  | LoweredLoop
  | LoweredLet
  | LoweredStatementSequence
  | LoweredPostfix
  | LoweredPrimary
  | LoweredFnDeclaration
  | LoweredTestDeclaration
  | LoweredDataDeclaration
  | LoweredFnBody
  | LoweredTypeDeclaration
  | LoweredServiceDeclaration
  | LoweredResourceDeclaration
  | LoweredOperand
